## Test

```bash
pytest
```

The component test boots the **same** app `{{ project_slug }}/startup.py` configures for a real
deployment, swaps the `Greeter` for a spy, then pushes a message through the whole Benzene pipeline
via the {% if transport == "aws-apigateway" %}API Gateway{% elif transport == "aws-sqs" %}SQS{% else %}gRPC{% endif %} front door and asserts the handler ran.

{% endif -%}
## Run / deploy

{% if transport == "aws-apigateway" -%}
Point your Lambda function's handler at `{{ project_slug }}.main.handler` and put an API Gateway HTTP
trigger in front of it. `GET /hello/{name}` returns a greeting. See the
[AWS host guide](https://github.com/daniellepelley/benzene-python/blob/main/examples/aws_orders).
{%- elif transport == "aws-sqs" -%}
Point your Lambda function's handler at `{{ project_slug }}.main.handler` and add an SQS event-source
mapping. Each message is routed by its `topic` message attribute to the matching handler; failures
are reported via the SQS partial-batch response. See the
[AWS host guide](https://github.com/daniellepelley/benzene-python/blob/main/examples/aws_orders).
{%- else -%}
```bash
python -m {{ project_slug }}.main      # serves on [::]:50051
```

Every Benzene topic is one generic gRPC unary method (`/benzene.Benzene/<topic>`). A client is a
`MessageSender` over a channel — see the
[gRPC example](https://github.com/daniellepelley/benzene-python/blob/main/examples/grpc_orders).
{%- endif %}

